  "reason": "The current best config (config_037: scvi_n200, vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.706 acc. The strongest evidence from RNA-only experiments shows avgpool (0.591) substantially outperforms transformer (0.519) aggregation, but this has not been confirmed in the multimodal regime with the top-performing encoders. Config_039 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other variables at their best-known values (scvi_n200, vit_l, multiprofile, weighted). This single-variable test will clarify whether the avgpool advantage persists with a stronger image encoder and weighted fusion, or whether transformer aggregation becomes competitive in the multimodal setting. If transformer underperforms (as expected), it confirms avgpool as the correct choice and directs remaining budget toward other unexplored axes. If transformer is competitive or better, it opens a new optimization direction. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a key architectural uncertainty at the top of the performance landscape with a clean, interpretable comparison."
